### 2. Per-Frame `preUpdate` Component Loop on Every Entity

**File:** [entity.js](file:///c:/work/mci-cognitive-games/src/game/symmetry-decor/entity/entity.js#L25-L32)

**Problem:** Every `Entity.preUpdate()` iterates over its `components[]` array and calls `component.update()` on each one **every frame**. Most components (`SocketComponent`, `DraggableComponent`, `DraggableDataComponent`, `NonDraggableComponent`, `SpriteRenderer`) have **empty `update()` methods** inherited from the base `Component` class, so this is pure overhead.

With ~72 entities × ~2 components each = **~144 no-op function calls per frame**.

**Impact:** Medium-high on mobile. Function call overhead + array iteration on every frame adds up.

**Fix:** Two options:
- **(A) Quick fix:** Only register components that actually define a meaningful `update()` in a separate `updatableComponents` array.
- **(B) Better fix:** Remove the `preUpdate` override entirely from `Entity` since no active component in this game uses `update()` (the `EmojiRenderer` does, but it's not used — the game uses `SpriteRenderer` instead).

