### 3. EventBus `minigame:tick` Emitted Every Frame

**File:** [Gameplay.js](file:///c:/work/mci-cognitive-games/src/game/symmetry-decor/scenes/Gameplay.js#L244)

**Problem:** `EventBus.emit('minigame:tick', ...)` is called **every single frame** (~60 times per second). This crosses the Phaser→React bridge, causing React state updates and potential re-renders on every frame.

**Impact:** High on mobile. React re-renders are expensive and the timer only needs to update once per second visually.

**Fix:** Only emit when `timeLeftS` actually changes (i.e., once per second):
```js
if (timeLeftS !== this._lastTimeLeftS) {
    this._lastTimeLeftS = timeLeftS;
    EventBus.emit('minigame:tick', { timeLeft: Math.max(0, timeLeftS), maxTime: maxTimeS });
}
```

