## 🟡 Moderate Issues

### 4. Excessive `console.log` in Hot Paths

**File:** [solutionSocket.js](file:///c:/work/mci-cognitive-games/src/game/symmetry-decor/components/scripts/solutionSocket.js#L15-L16)

**Problem:** `SolutionSocketComponent.checkEntity()` logs **two `console.log` calls** every time it's invoked. This method is called during every drop event and during the `checkIfAllSocketIsFilledCorrectly()` loop (which iterates all solution slots). Console logging is synchronous and surprisingly expensive on mobile browsers.

**Impact:** Moderate. Each drop triggers many `checkEntity` calls across all solution slots.

**Fix:** Remove or gate behind a debug flag:
```js
checkEntity(entity) {
    if (entity == null) return false;
    return entity.type === this.type && entity.animal === this.animal;
}
```

---

### 5. Grid Background Drawing Creates Too Many Graphics Objects

**File:** [entityGrid.js](file:///c:/work/mci-cognitive-games/src/game/symmetry-decor/entity/entityGrid.js#L191-L254)

**Problem:** `drawGridBackground()` calls `graphics.beginPath()` + `graphics.strokePath()` in a **per-segment loop** for every inner grid line. On a 6x6 grid, this creates dozens of individual draw calls. Additionally, `drawSymmetryLine()` creates a separate `Graphics` object with its own dashed-line path.

**Impact:** Moderate on mobile. Each `beginPath/strokePath` pair generates a separate WebGL draw call. Mobile GPUs have much lower draw-call budgets than desktop.

**Fix:** Batch all same-color line segments into a **single** `beginPath/strokePath` call. Group reference-colored lines and normal-colored lines separately:
```js
// Instead of per-segment beginPath/strokePath:
graphicsBorders.lineStyle(innerBorderThickness, innerBorderColor, 1.0);
graphicsBorders.beginPath();
// ... all normal-color moveTo/lineTo calls ...
graphicsBorders.strokePath();

graphicsBorders.lineStyle(innerBorderThickness, refBorderColor, 1.0);
graphicsBorders.beginPath();
// ... all ref-color moveTo/lineTo calls ...
graphicsBorders.strokePath();
```

